IMPORTANT:
Do NOT delete the current General settings.
Do NOT remove Animations.
Do NOT remove Open App Directly to Chat.
Do NOT replace the existing native/iOS-style popups, sheets, or selection menus.
Keep the current iOS interaction behavior exactly as it is where it already works.

The goal is to:
1. Organize Settings better.
2. Add the missing important sections.
3. Make the settings actually functional.
4. Connect real settings to the backend / authenticated user profile where appropriate.
5. Preserve the current iOS UI/UX system.

====================================================
1. GENERAL
====================================================

Keep the existing General page.

Current settings such as:

- Open App Directly to Chat
- Animations

must remain.

Do NOT delete them.

You may improve spacing/layout so the rows have more room and the text does not feel compressed.

Also add useful real General settings if the current architecture supports them, such as:

- Default Start Screen
- Haptics
- App behavior preferences

Do not add fake settings.

Every added option must either:
- work now, or
- remain clearly disabled/unavailable until implemented.

For settings with multiple choices:
continue using the same existing iOS-style popup/sheet selector.

For simple On/Off settings:
use the same current interaction pattern already established in BlueMind.

