2. SECURITY & LOGIN
====================================================

Add a new dedicated section:

SECURITY & LOGIN

This must NOT be mixed into General.

It should include real account/security controls such as:

- Face ID Lock
- Change Password
- Sign-in Methods
- Active Sessions / Devices
- Log out of other devices

If a feature is supported by the backend, connect it properly.

Face ID Lock:
- must use LocalAuthentication
- must use the existing authenticated session
- must not become a separate login provider
- must persist correctly
- must not bypass invalid/expired backend sessions

Change Password:
- use the real existing backend password-change flow
- verify the current authenticated user
- do not fake success locally

Sign-in Methods:
- show the real providers linked to the account, such as:
  - Email/password
  - Google
  - Apple
- use real backend/provider state

Active Sessions / Devices:
- only show real session/device data if available from backend
- do not invent devices

Log out of other devices:
- only enable if supported by backend/session architecture
- revoke the appropriate sessions server-side

