====================================================
7. BACKEND / DATA CONNECTION
====================================================

This is important.

Audit every Settings item and classify it as:

A. Local device preference
B. User account preference
C. Backend security/account action
D. iOS system permission

Store it in the correct place.

Examples:

Local/device:
- animation preference
- haptics
- appearance

Account/backend:
- password
- linked login providers
- privacy preferences
- session management

iOS system:
- Face ID availability
- notification authorization

Do NOT store everything in localStorage just because it is easier.

Use:
- Keychain for sensitive session/auth material
- backend/database for account-specific preferences/actions
- appropriate local persistent storage for non-sensitive device preferences
- native iOS APIs for system permissions

